{"title": "Sectional Mock #1 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The length, breadth and height of a cuboid are 16 m, 14m and 2&radic;31m respectively. Find the length of diagonal of the cuboid.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 16 m, 14 m &#2324;&#2352; 2&radic;31 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["19 m", "23 m", "21 m", "24 m"], "options_hi": ["19 m", "23 m", "21 m", "24 m"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=385 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=151 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=131 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image029.png\"></p><p><img width=52 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image031.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=385 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=151 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=131 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image029.png\"></p><p><img width=52 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image031.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 5<sup>3a + 2b </sup>= 625 and 7<sup>2a + b </sup>= 49, then find the value of 'b'.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 5<sup>3a + 2b </sup>= 625 &#2324;&#2352; 7<sup>2a + b </sup>= 49 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'b' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here, 5<sup>3a + 2b </sup>= 625</p><p>5<sup>3a + 2b </sup>= 5<sup>4</sup></p><p>3a + 2b = 4 =&gt; a = (4  -  2b)/3 ...(i)</p><p>And 7<sup>2a + b </sup>= 49</p><p>7<sup>2a + b </sup>= 7<sup>2</sup></p><p>2a + b = 2 =&gt; a = (2  -  b)/2 ...(ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii)), we have</p><p>(4  -  2b)/3 = (2  -  b)/2</p><p>2(4  -  2b) = 3(2  -  b)</p><p>8  -  4b = 6  -  3b</p><p><b>b = 2</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, 5<sup>3a + 2b </sup>= 625</p><p>5<sup>3a + 2b </sup>= 5<sup>4</sup></p><p>3a + 2b = 4 =&gt; a = (4  -  2b)/3 ...(i)</p><p>And 7<sup>2a + b </sup>= 49</p><p>7<sup>2a + b </sup>= 7<sup>2</sup></p><p>2a + b = 2 =&gt; a = (2  -  b)/2 ...(ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii)), we have</p><p>(4  -  2b)/3 = (2  -  b)/2</p><p>2(4  -  2b) = 3(2  -  b)</p><p>8  -  4b = 6  -  3b</p><p><b>b = 2</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average of thirty  -  five numbers is 60. The average of the first 18 numbers and that of the last 18 numbers is 54.2 and 70.8 respectively. If the 18<sup>th</sup> number is excluded, then what is the average of the remaining numbers (correct to one decimal place)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2376;&#2306;&#2340;&#2368;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 60 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; 18 &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; 18 &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 54.2 &#2324;&#2352; 70.8 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 18&#2357;&#2368;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; (&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["52.5", "57.3", "60.7", "59.9"], "options_hi": ["52.5", "57.3", "60.7", "59.9"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>18<sup>th</sup> number = (Sum of first 18 numbers + Sum of last 18 numbers) - Sum of 35 numbers </p><p>= 18*54.2 + 18*70.8  -  35*60</p><p>= 18*125  -  2100</p><p>= 150</p><p>Average of the remaining 34 numbers = (35*60  -  150)/34 = 57.3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>18<sup>th</sup> number = (Sum of first 18 numbers + Sum of last 18 numbers) - Sum of 35 numbers </p><p>= 18*54.2 + 18*70.8  -  35*60</p><p>= 18*125  -  2100</p><p>= 150</p><p>Average of the remaining 34 numbers = (35*60  -  150)/34 = 57.3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>The arithmetic mean of the following data is:</p><p>23, 17, 20, 19, 21</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2327;&#2339;&#2367;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p>23, 17, 20, 19, 21</p>", "options_en": ["20", "19", "23", "21"], "options_hi": ["20", "19", "23", "21"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The arithmetic mean = (23 + 17 + 20 + 19 + 21) /5 = 20</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The arithmetic mean = (23 + 17 + 20 + 19 + 21) /5 = 20</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p> If <i>x</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9, <i>y</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 16 and <i>z</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 144, then what is <i>x</i> equal to? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; <i>x</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9, <i>y</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 16 &#2324;&#2352; <i>z</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 144 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; <i>x</i> &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["9/5", "9/7", "9/13", "16/13"], "options_hi": ["9/5", "9/7", "9/13", "16/13"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>\"</p><p>From question, <i>x</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9, <i>y</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 16 and <i>z</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 144</p><p>Adding all equations, we get</p><p>( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> )( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9 + 16 + 144</p><p>&#8594; ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) <sup>2</sup> = 169</p><p>&#8594; <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> = 13</p><p>&#8756; <i>x</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9</p><p><i>x</i> (13) = 9</p><p><i>x</i> = 9/13</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>\"</p><p>From question, <i>x</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9, <i>y</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 16 and <i>z</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 144</p><p>Adding all equations, we get</p><p>( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> )( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9 + 16 + 144</p><p>&#8594; ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) <sup>2</sup> = 169</p><p>&#8594; <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> = 13</p><p>&#8756; <i>x</i> ( <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i> ) = 9</p><p><i>x</i> (13) = 9</p><p><i>x</i> = 9/13</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a race of three oxen Heera, Moti and Ramu, Heera beats Moti by 12 metres and Ramu by 87 metres. If Moti beat Ramu by 76 metres, what was the length of the race course?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2348;&#2376;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2368;&#2352;&#2366;, &#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2368;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2370; &#2325;&#2379; 87 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2370; &#2325;&#2379; 76 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["912 m", "884 m", "900 m", "880 m"], "options_hi": ["912 &#2350;&#2368;", "884 &#2350;&#2368;", "900 &#2350;&#2368;", "880 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the length of race course = L meters</p><p>Distance covered by Heera = L meters</p><p>Distance covered by Moti = 'L  -  12' meters</p><p>Distance covered by Ramu = 'L  -  87' meters</p><p>and</p><p>Distance covered by Moti = L meters</p><p>Distance covered by Ramu = 'L  -  76' meters</p><p>Now,</p><p>(L  -  12)/(L  -  87) = L/(L  -  76)</p><p>L<sup>2</sup>  -  88L + 912 = L<sup>2</sup>  -  87L</p><p>L = 912 </p><p>Therefore, length of race course = 912 meters</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length of race course = L meters</p><p>Distance covered by Heera = L meters</p><p>Distance covered by Moti = 'L  -  12' meters</p><p>Distance covered by Ramu = 'L  -  87' meters</p><p>and</p><p>Distance covered by Moti = L meters</p><p>Distance covered by Ramu = 'L  -  76' meters</p><p>Now,</p><p>(L  -  12)/(L  -  87) = L/(L  -  76)</p><p>L<sup>2</sup>  -  88L + 912 = L<sup>2</sup>  -  87L</p><p>L = 912 </p><p>Therefore, length of race course = 912 meters</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of X, if 50% of 120 x 2/3 of 60  -  (50 + 120  -  30 <img width=12 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image027.png\"> 3) = 20X</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 120 &#2325;&#2366; 50% x 60 &#2325;&#2366; 2/3 - (50 + 120 - 30 <img width=12 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image027.png\"> 3) = 20X</p>", "options_en": ["134", "144", "112", "124"], "options_hi": ["134", "144", "112", "124"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>50% of 120 x 2/3 of 60  -  (50 + 120  -  30 <img width=12 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image027.png\"> 3) = 20X</p><p>60 x 40  -  (50 + 120  -  10) = 20X</p><p>2400  -  160 = 20X</p><p>X = 112</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>50% of 120 x 2/3 of 60  -  (50 + 120  -  30 <img width=12 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image027.png\"> 3) = 20X</p><p>60 x 40  -  (50 + 120  -  10) = 20X</p><p>2400  -  160 = 20X</p><p>X = 112</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person deposited some amount of money in the bank at simple interest. After 20 years, the amount became nine times the amount deposited. In how many years will the amount become 13 times the amount if the interest rate remains the same?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; 20 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2380; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2312;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361;&#2368; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 13 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["30", "25", "28", "23"], "options_hi": ["30", "25", "28", "23"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let principal = &#8377;P</p><p>P(1 + 20R/100) = 9P</p><p>1 + R/5 = 9</p><p>R/5 = 8</p><p>R = 40%</p><p>Now,</p><p>P(1 + 40T/100) = 13P</p><p>1 + 2T/5 = 13</p><p>2T/5 = 12</p><p>T = 30 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let principal = &#8377;P</p><p>P(1 + 20R/100) = 9P</p><p>1 + R/5 = 9</p><p>R/5 = 8</p><p>R = 40%</p><p>Now,</p><p>P(1 + 40T/100) = 13P</p><p>1 + 2T/5 = 13</p><p>2T/5 = 12</p><p>T = 30 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>20 persons started a work together, but after some days, 8 persons leave. As a result, the job, which could have been completed in 80 days, was completed in 100 days. How many days after commencement of the work did the four persons leave?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>20 &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 8 &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2347;&#2354;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; 80 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;, &#2357;&#2361; 100 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310;&#2404; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["50", "48", "60", "40"], "options_hi": ["50", "48", "60", "40"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of days be X after which the four persons leave the work after commencement.</p><p>Total work = 20 * 80 units</p><p>Total work = [20X + 12(100  -  X)] units</p><p>Now,</p><p>1600 = 20X + 1200  -  12X</p><p>400 = 8X</p><p>X = 50</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of days be X after which the four persons leave the work after commencement.</p><p>Total work = 20 * 80 units</p><p>Total work = [20X + 12(100  -  X)] units</p><p>Now,</p><p>1600 = 20X + 1200  -  12X</p><p>400 = 8X</p><p>X = 50</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of (1 + cotA  -  cosecA)(1 + tanA + secA)  -  3(sin<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>A).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(1 + cotA - cosecA)(1 + tanA + secA) - 3(sin<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>A) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["-1", "1", "2", "-2"], "options_hi": ["-1", "1", "2", "-2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>(1 + cotA  -  cosecA)(1 + tanA + secA)  -  3(sin<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>A)</p><p>= (1 + tanA + secA + cotA + cotA tanA + cotA secA  -  cosecA  -  cosecA tanA  -  cosecA secA)  -  3*1</p><p>= 1 + tanA + secA + cotA + 1 + cosecA  -  cosecA  -  secA  -  cosecA secA  -  3</p><p>= tanA + cotA  -  cosecA secA  -  1</p><p>= sinA/cosA + cosA/sinA  -  1/sinAcosA  -  1</p><p>= (sin<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>A)/sinAcosA  -  1/sinAcosA  -  1</p><p>= 1/sinAcosA  -  1/sinAcosA  -  1</p><p>= -1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(1 + cotA  -  cosecA)(1 + tanA + secA)  -  3(sin<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>A)</p><p>= (1 + tanA + secA + cotA + cotA tanA + cotA secA  -  cosecA  -  cosecA tanA  -  cosecA secA)  -  3*1</p><p>= 1 + tanA + secA + cotA + 1 + cosecA  -  cosecA  -  secA  -  cosecA secA  -  3</p><p>= tanA + cotA  -  cosecA secA  -  1</p><p>= sinA/cosA + cosA/sinA  -  1/sinAcosA  -  1</p><p>= (sin<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>A)/sinAcosA  -  1/sinAcosA  -  1</p><p>= 1/sinAcosA  -  1/sinAcosA  -  1</p><p>= -1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>A die is cast twice and a coin is tossed thrice. Find the probability that the die will turn a 5 each time and the coin will turn a head every time.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2331;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2331;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2348;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; 5 &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1/50", "1/200", "1/100", "1/288"], "options_hi": ["1/50", "1/200", "1/100", "1/288"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Die P(5) = 1/6, twice = (1/6) * (1/6) = 1/36</p><p>Coin P(H) = 1/2, thrice = (1/2)^3 = 1/8</p><p>Total = (1/36) * (1/8) = 1/288</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Die P(5) = 1/6, twice = (1/6) * (1/6) = 1/36</p><p>Coin P(H) = 1/2, thrice = (1/2)^3 = 1/8</p><p>Total = (1/36) * (1/8) = 1/288</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>Height of a tower is 120m.The angle of elevation of the top of tower from a point B is 75&#176;. Point B is on the ground level. What is the distance of point B from the base of tower?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 120 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 75&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; B &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367;-&#2340;&#2354; (&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2313;&#2306;&#2337;-&#2354;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354;) &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2379;, &#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["120(2-&#8730;3)", "180(3-&#8730;3)", "180(&#8730;3-1)", "190(&#8730;3-1)"], "options_hi": ["120(2-&radic;3)", "180(3-&radic;3)", "180(&radic;3-1)", "190(&radic;3-1)"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/8a1f3a8652d34dd27e294a7026673684.png\" /> </p><p>Let AC be the tower. </p><p> Required distance , BA = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/4a8e7c0c78b96cbd4ef19586b0a04357.png\" /> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005173.png\"/></p><p> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005441.png\"/></p><p> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005614.png\"/></p><p> </p>", "solution_hi": "<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/8a1f3a8652d34dd27e294a7026673684.png\" /> </p><p>Let AC be the tower. </p><p> Required distance , BA = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/4a8e7c0c78b96cbd4ef19586b0a04357.png\" /> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005173.png\"/></p><p> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005441.png\"/></p><p> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005614.png\"/></p><p> </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two vessels, A and B, contain spirit and water in the ratio 3:4 and 5:3, respectively. Find the ratio in which these two mixtures be mixed to obtain a new mixture in vessel C containing spirit and water in the ratio 4:3.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3:4 &#2324;&#2352; 5:3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; C &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:3 &#2361;&#2379;, &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3:8", "3:7", "5:8", "4:7"], "options_hi": ["3:8", "3:7", "5:8", "4:7"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Vessel A: Spirit = 3/7, Water = 4/7 </p><p>Vessel B: Spirit = 5/8, Water = 3/8 </p><p>Desired: Spirit = 4/7, Water = 3/7 </p><p>Using allegation on spirit: </p><p>(5/8 - 4/7) / (4/7 - 3/7) </p><p>LCM of 8, 7 = 56 </p><p>5/8 = 35/56, 4/7 = 32/56, 3/7 = 24/56 </p><p>(35/56 - 32/56) : (32/56 - 24/56) </p><p>(3/56) : (8/56) = 3:8 </p><p>Ratio of A:B = 3:8</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Vessel A: Spirit = 3/7, Water = 4/7 </p><p>Vessel B: Spirit = 5/8, Water = 3/8 </p><p>Desired: Spirit = 4/7, Water = 3/7 </p><p>Using allegation on spirit: </p><p>(5/8 - 4/7) / (4/7 - 3/7) </p><p>LCM of 8, 7 = 56 </p><p>5/8 = 35/56, 4/7 = 32/56, 3/7 = 24/56 </p><p>(35/56 - 32/56) : (32/56 - 24/56) </p><p>(3/56) : (8/56) = 3:8 </p><p>Ratio of A:B = 3:8</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many times is 0.5 greater than 0.002?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>0.5, 0.002 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["300", "200", "150", "250"], "options_hi": ["300", "200", "150", "250"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=43 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image002.png\"></p><p>= 7 + (328  -  32)/900</p><p>= 7 + 296/900</p><p>= 6596/900 = 1649/225</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=43 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image002.png\"></p><p>= 7 + (328  -  32)/900</p><p>= 7 + 296/900</p><p>= 6596/900 = 1649/225</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ramesh purchased 130 books at the rate of &#8377;200 each and sold half of them at the rate of &#8377;300 each, one-fifth of them at the rate of &#8377;350 each and the rest at the cost price. Find his profit percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2350;&#2375;&#2358; &#2344;&#2375; 130 &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;200 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;300 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#8377;350 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["35%", "40%", "38%", "44%"], "options_hi": ["35%", "40%", "38%", "44%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total cost price = 130 * 200 = &#8377;26000</p><p>Selling price of 65 books = 65 * 300 = &#8377;19500</p><p>Selling price of 130/5 or 26 books = 26 * 350 = &#8377;9100</p><p>Selling price of remaining 39 books = 39 * 200 = &#8377;7800</p><p>Total selling price = 19500 + 9100 + 7800 = 36400</p><p>Profit percentage = (36400  -  26000)/26000 * 100 = 40%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total cost price = 130 * 200 = &#8377;26000</p><p>Selling price of 65 books = 65 * 300 = &#8377;19500</p><p>Selling price of 130/5 or 26 books = 26 * 350 = &#8377;9100</p><p>Selling price of remaining 39 books = 39 * 200 = &#8377;7800</p><p>Total selling price = 19500 + 9100 + 7800 = 36400</p><p>Profit percentage = (36400  -  26000)/26000 * 100 = 40%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>There are two pipes used to fill a tank and when operated together, they can fill the tank in 20 minutes. If one pipe can fill the tank two and a half times as quickly as the other, then the faster pipe alone can fill the tank in:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2348; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; 20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2338;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:", "options_en": ["30 min", "32 min", "34 min", "28 min"], "options_hi": ["30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "32 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "34 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "28 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the two pipes be x and y</p><p>They can fill together in 20 minutes.</p><p>Let efficiency of x&gt;y</p><p>So efficiency of x/y=2.5/1=5/2</p><p>Let efficiency of x = 5k and for y =2k</p><p>So total work=(5k+2k)*20</p><p>So faster one can fill it in= 7k*20/5k=28 min.</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the two pipes be x and y</p><p>They can fill together in 20 minutes.</p><p>Let efficiency of x&gt;y</p><p>So efficiency of x/y=2.5/1=5/2</p><p>Let efficiency of x = 5k and for y =2k</p><p>So total work=(5k+2k)*20</p><p>So faster one can fill it in= 7k*20/5k=28 min.</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the HCF of 7, 2.8, and 0.14.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>7, 2.8 &#2324;&#2352; 0.14 &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["0.7", "0.14", "1.4", "7"], "options_hi": ["0.7", "0.14", "1.4", "7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>We can write 7, 2.8, and 0.14 as 7.00, 2.80, and 0.14 respectively.</p><p>After leaving the decimals, we have 700, 280, and 14.</p><p>And 700 and 280 both are divisible by 14.</p><p>Therefore, the required HCF (with added decimal) will be 0.14.</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We can write 7, 2.8, and 0.14 as 7.00, 2.80, and 0.14 respectively.</p><p>After leaving the decimals, we have 700, 280, and 14.</p><p>And 700 and 280 both are divisible by 14.</p><p>Therefore, the required HCF (with added decimal) will be 0.14.</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sample A contains two types of sugars costing Rs.50 per kg and Rs.40 per kg in the ratio 3:7 respectively and sample B contains two types of sugars costing Rs.50 per kg and Rs.40 per kg in the ratio 2:3 respectively. In what ratio these two samples should be mixed, so that final mixture contains sugars costing Rs.50 per kg and Rs.40 per kg in the ratio 9:16 respectively?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2350;&#2370;&#2344;&#2366; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 50 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3:7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2350;&#2370;&#2344;&#2366; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 50 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2:3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2350;&#2370;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 50 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 9:16 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["1:3", "2:3", "4:5", "3:7"], "options_hi": ["1:3", "2:3", "4:5", "3:7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Percentage of sugar costing Rs.50 per kg in sample A</p><p>= (3/10) x 100% = 30%</p><p>Percentage of sugar costing Rs.50 per kg in sample B</p><p>= (2/5) x 100% = 40%</p><p>Percentage of sugar costing Rs.50 per kg in final mixture</p><p>= (9/25) x 100% = 36%</p><p>According to Alligation rule,</p><p><img width=178 height=140 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5093/image005.jpg\"></p><p>Ratio = 4/6 = 2:3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Percentage of sugar costing Rs.50 per kg in sample A</p><p>= (3/10) x 100% = 30%</p><p>Percentage of sugar costing Rs.50 per kg in sample B</p><p>= (2/5) x 100% = 40%</p><p>Percentage of sugar costing Rs.50 per kg in final mixture</p><p>= (9/25) x 100% = 36%</p><p>According to Alligation rule,</p><p><img width=178 height=140 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5093/image005.jpg\"></p><p>Ratio = 4/6 = 2:3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>MNOP is a trapezium such that PO || MN, &#8736; PMN = 80&deg; and PM = ON. Find the measure of &#8736; ONM.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>MNOP &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; PO || MN, &#8736; PMN = 80&deg; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; PM = ON &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736; ONM &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["40&deg;", "100&deg;", "80&deg;", "60&deg;"], "options_hi": ["40&deg;", "100&deg;", "80&deg;", "60&deg;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=249 height=169 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image013.png\"></p><p>Given, PM = ON, therefore trapezium MNOP is an isosceles trapezium.</p><p>Therefore, &#8736; ONM = &#8736; PMN = 80&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=249 height=169 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image013.png\"></p><p>Given, PM = ON, therefore trapezium MNOP is an isosceles trapezium.</p><p>Therefore, &#8736; ONM = &#8736; PMN = 80&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A mango seller makes a profit of 30% by selling Alphonso mangoes at a certain price. If he charges Rs 2 more per Alphonso, he would gain 50%. Find the original price of mango?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2350; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2306;&#2360;&#2379; &#2310;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2325;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2306;&#2360;&#2379; &#2310;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; 2 &#2352;&#2369; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2358;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 50% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;| &#2310;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs 12", "Rs 10", "Rs 11", "Rs 18"], "options_hi": ["12 &#2352;&#2369;", "10 &#2352;&#2369;", "11 &#2352;&#2369;", "18 &#2352;&#2369;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the original price of mango be X.</p><p>Now it is given that if we add Rs 2 to the selling price, the profit will get an increase from 30% to 50%.</p><p>Therefore we can say that 20% = Rs 2.</p><p>So the original price of mango, i.e 100% = (100  *  2)/20 = Rs 10</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the original price of mango be X.</p><p>Now it is given that if we add Rs 2 to the selling price, the profit will get an increase from 30% to 50%.</p><p>Therefore we can say that 20% = Rs 2.</p><p>So the original price of mango, i.e 100% = (100  *  2)/20 = Rs 10</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If 5x + <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 5x + <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "options_en": ["77", "76", "78", "75"], "options_hi": ["77", "76", "78", "75"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=109 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=80 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=195 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=165 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=109 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=80 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=195 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=165 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22687/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sum of digits of a 3-digit number is 13 and its unit digit is 3 times of the digit at hundreds place. If unit digit is 1 more than tens digit, then find the number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; 3-&#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 13 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2360;&#2376;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; 3 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2342;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["256", "247", "319", "283"], "options_hi": ["256", "247", "319", "283"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let 3-digit number = 100a + 10b + c</p><p>(a + b + c) = 13 ...... (1)</p><p>c = 3a ...... (2)</p><p>c  -  b = 1</p><p>b = c  -  1 = 3a  -  1 ...... (3)</p><p>From (1), (2) and (3):</p><p>a + (3a  -  1) + 3a = 13</p><p>=> a = 2</p><p>b = 3a  -  1 = 5</p><p>c = 3a = 6</p><p>Number = 100a + 10b + c</p><p>= 200 + 50 + 6</p><p>= 256</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let 3-digit number = 100a + 10b + c</p><p>(a + b + c) = 13 ...... (1)</p><p>c = 3a ...... (2)</p><p>c  -  b = 1</p><p>b = c  -  1 = 3a  -  1 ...... (3)</p><p>From (1), (2) and (3):</p><p>a + (3a  -  1) + 3a = 13</p><p>=> a = 2</p><p>b = 3a  -  1 = 5</p><p>c = 3a = 6</p><p>Number = 100a + 10b + c</p><p>= 200 + 50 + 6</p><p>= 256</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A mixture of 750 kg of alloy of copper and tin contains 25% tin. How much tin must be added so that it becomes 70% of the mixture?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; 750 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 25% &#2335;&#2367;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2335;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; 70% &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["895 kg", "1125 kg", "956 kg", "1097 kg"], "options_hi": ["895 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "1125 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "956 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "1097 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Original quantity of tin = 25% of 750 = 187.5 kg</p><p>Let quantity of tin added = x kg</p><p>Now,</p><p>(187.5 + x)/(750 + x) = 70/100</p><p>1875 + 10x = 5250 + 7x</p><p>3x = 3375</p><p>x = 1125 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Original quantity of tin = 25% of 750 = 187.5 kg</p><p>Let quantity of tin added = x kg</p><p>Now,</p><p>(187.5 + x)/(750 + x) = 70/100</p><p>1875 + 10x = 5250 + 7x</p><p>3x = 3375</p><p>x = 1125 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of number of sides of two regular polygons is 2:3. If the sum of one polygon's interior angles is added to the sum of the other polygon's interior angles, then the added value will be 1080&deg;. The measures of their exterior angles are  - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2:3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;: &#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;: &#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; 1080&deg; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2361;&#2367;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; -</p>", "options_en": ["80&deg;, 60", "90&deg;, 45&deg;", "100&deg;, 60&deg;", "90&deg;, 60&deg;"], "options_hi": ["80&deg;, 60", "90&deg;, 45&deg;", "100&deg;, 60&deg;", "90&deg;, 60&deg;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let, the number of sides of two regular polygons be n<sub>1</sub> and n<sub>2</sub>.</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/n<sub>2 </sub>= 2/3</p><p>[(n<sub>1 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] + [(n<sub>2 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] = 1080&deg;</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub> -  2 + n<sub>2</sub>  -  2 = 1080/180 = 6</p><p>n<sub>1</sub> + n<sub>2 </sub>= 10</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>+ 3n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>5n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 2</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>= 4</p><p>So, n<sub>2 </sub>= 6</p><p>Exterior angle of one polygon = 360/4 = 90&deg;</p><p>Exterior angle of the other polygon = 360/6 = 60&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the number of sides of two regular polygons be n<sub>1</sub> and n<sub>2</sub>.</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/n<sub>2 </sub>= 2/3</p><p>[(n<sub>1 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] + [(n<sub>2 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] = 1080&deg;</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub> -  2 + n<sub>2</sub>  -  2 = 1080/180 = 6</p><p>n<sub>1</sub> + n<sub>2 </sub>= 10</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>+ 3n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>5n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 2</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>= 4</p><p>So, n<sub>2 </sub>= 6</p><p>Exterior angle of one polygon = 360/4 = 90&deg;</p><p>Exterior angle of the other polygon = 360/6 = 60&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Anamika paid &#8377;4,965 as compound interest on a loan of &#8377;15,000 after 3 years when compounded annually. Suman took a loan of &#8377;10,000 at the same rate on simple interest. How much interest did Suman pay after 3 years?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#8377; 15,000 &#2325;&#2375; &#2315;&#2339; &#2346;&#2352; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377; 4,965 &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2360;&#2369;&#2350;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#8377; 10,000 &#2325;&#2366; &#2315;&#2339; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2360;&#2369;&#2350;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;3,000", "&#8377;3,500", "&#8377;4,500", "&#8377;4,000"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;3,000", "&#8377;3,500", "&#8377;4,500", "&#8377;4,000"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Amount paid by Anamika = 15000 + 4965 = Rs. 19965</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><img width=173 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image120.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image121.png\"></p><p><img width=113 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image122.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image123.png\"></p><p><img width=43 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image124.png\"></p><p>Rate of interest for Suman = 10%</p><p>Simple interest paid by Suman = 10000 * 3 * 10/100 = Rs. 3000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount paid by Anamika = 15000 + 4965 = Rs. 19965</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><img width=173 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image120.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image121.png\"></p><p><img width=113 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image122.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image123.png\"></p><p><img width=43 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image124.png\"></p><p>Rate of interest for Suman = 10%</p><p>Simple interest paid by Suman = 10000 * 3 * 10/100 = Rs. 3000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}]}